Some of the other people here responded to this message in a somewhat
snarky manner.  I don't think any of us are done any favors by this
behavior.

Whenever I see a long message like this from a new Nethack player, what
I see is someone full of energy and love for the game, and wants his
friends to also enjoy it.  When I see someone post yet another YANI, I
see someone wanting to contribute.  Nethack is a game built off of the
ideas of hundreds of people.  Even if an idea is misguided (and I don't
think that's always an easy decision to make), getting the idea out
there helps us all in the end.

This having been said, I think that perhaps your friends are not as
close to enjoying Nethack as you think they are.  Even if it had the
best possible interface, lots of people weaned on console RPGs will
probably require at least a mid-level epiphany before they will see
what's great about Nethack.  Nethack is a game that requires you earn a
B.A. in it in order to do well; most common gamers these days will run
to a strategy guide or GameFAQs the moment something happens in a game
that they have to figure out.  Their idea of "playing" tends to be
using the same button combinations over and over, for the entire game.
Once they get tired of *that*, they just might be ready for Nethack.


