This may be interesting to new players, but most Nethack veterans would
just get bogged down by it.

This may be part of the disconnect here, between yourself and the group
regulars.  Nethack is a game of many wonderous design elements.  Most
other games have, when it comes right down to it, fairly lightweight
gameplay.  So lightweight, in fact, that the graphical splendor,
detailed models and animations are mostly there to distract you from
the intellectual paucity of the thing.

Nethack, on the other hand, doesn't need those distractions.  It
doesn't even need a *story*: the game is interesting enough, in its
wealth of options available to the player and extreme cleverness of
design, that it is compelling all by itself.

Just because it doesn't need them doesn't mean they wouldn't be nice to
have.  But again, it'd probably be something you'd have to work on
yourself.


